# Density Compare
# Carbon (C) — real density 2.267 g/cm³. equal masses: Carbon vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Carbon Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 15.2mm material: carbon at (-20mm, 7.6mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 18.1 g — the water cube is the reference
